{
  "title": "Apollo MCP Server Dashboard Template",
  "description": null,
  "widgets": [
    {
      "id": 288835591938150,
      "definition": {
        "title": "$service #$env",
        "type": "trace_service",
        "env": "$env",
        "service": "$service",
        "span_name": "",
        "show_hits": true,
        "show_errors": true,
        "show_latency": true,
        "show_breakdown": true,
        "show_distribution": true,
        "show_resource_list": false,
        "size_format": "medium",
        "display_format": "two_column"
      },
      "layout": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "height": 11
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "**APM hits count most MCP requests twice.** Datadog names both the HTTP span and the MCP handler span `http.server.request`, so a request that reaches a handler, such as `tools/call`, has two hits. With the server's default `parent_based_sampler: true`, hits also leave out every request whose caller sends trace flags `00`. Count requests with the metric widgets below, and set `telemetry.exporters.tracing.parent_based_sampler: false` to trace every request.",
        "background_color": "yellow",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "vertical_align": "top",
        "show_tick": false,
        "tick_pos": "50%",
        "tick_edge": "left",
        "has_padding": true
      },
      "layout": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11,
        "width": 12,
        "height": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "show_title": true,
        "title": "MCP Requests",
        "type": "group",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "note",
              "content": "Built on `mcp.server.operation.duration` from the OpenTelemetry MCP semantic conventions (Apollo MCP Server v2.2.0 and later). The conventions are experimental, so these names can change in a minor release. The latency widgets leave out `subscriptions/listen`, which measures how long a client listened rather than request latency.",
              "background_color": "gray",
              "font_size": "14",
              "text_align": "left",
              "vertical_align": "top",
              "show_tick": false,
              "tick_pos": "50%",
              "tick_edge": "left",
              "has_padding": true
            },
            "layout": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 0,
              "width": 12,
              "height": 2
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
              "legend_columns": [
                "avg",
                "min",
                "max",
                "value",
                "sum"
              ],
              "legend_layout": "auto",
              "requests": [
                {
                  "display_type": "bars",
                  "formulas": [
                    {
                      "formula": "query1"
                    }
                  ],
                  "queries": [
                    {
                      "data_source": "metrics",
                      "name": "query1",
                      "query": "count:mcp.server.operation.duration{$service, $env} by {mcp.method.name}.as_count()"
                    }
                  ],
                  "response_format": "timeseries",
                  "style": {
                    "line_type": "solid",
                    "line_width": "normal",
                    "order_by": "values",
                    "palette": "dog_classic"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "show_legend": true,
              "title": "Requests by MCP method",
              "title_align": "left",
              "title_size": "16",
              "type": "timeseries"
            },
            "layout": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 2,
              "width": 6,
              "height": 3
            }
          },
          {
            "definition": {
